Semiconductors are often referred to as the oil of the

00:41:14.959 --> 00:41:16.019
21st century,

00:41:16.040 --> 00:41:19.879
The one raw material, so to speak, on which

00:41:19.879 --> 00:41:21.319
almost everything else depends.

00:41:22.220 --> 00:41:23.620
By 2030 we want,

00:41:23.620 --> 00:41:24.860
together with our industries,.

00:41:25.800 --> 00:41:27.699
to double Europe's share of the

00:41:27.699 --> 00:41:29.040
worldwide semiconductor production

00:41:29.040 --> 00:41:31.220
to 20 percent.

00:41:31.919 --> 00:41:33.540
And because the semiconductor market

00:41:33.540 --> 00:41:35.540
is developing so rapidly,

00:41:35.860 --> 00:41:37.139
it actually means for us?

00:41:37.680 --> 00:41:39.279
that our current capacities

00:41:39.279 --> 00:41:41.000
need to quadruple.

00:41:42.180 --> 00:41:43.919
43 billion Euros

00:41:43.919 --> 00:41:48.220
the EU provides for this.
Under these conditions

00:41:48.220 --> 00:41:49.599
Dresden is also

00:41:49.599 --> 00:41:51.779
attractive for TSMC.

00:41:52.940 --> 00:41:54.000
A fool who thinks

00:41:54.000 --> 00:41:54.699
that Taiwan's

00:41:54.699 --> 00:41:55.699
most important company

00:41:55.699 --> 00:41:57.599
